From 54619460d42712fbfe687f56bab491f22ddbe97b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Viktor Semenov <suit.uanic@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Mar 2026 16:46:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] Route AI through network and fix non-host saves

This also allows to rejoin multiplayer games with AI.

Only the controller (host) runs AI computation.
Non-host clients skip AI entirely via SetAISkipped.
AI commands route through PostNetworkCommand so all
clients receive them via the server. The server
validates that the controller may only send commands
for unassigned (AI) players.

Non-host clients fetch the controller's full game
state before saving, ensuring AI state is preserved.
The save request reuses the existing REJOIN file
transfer path: the server requests serialized state
from the controller, then forwards it to the
requesting client, which strips the turn prefix and
writes the save.

AIManager and AIInterface components are excluded
from the state hash since AI state diverges across
clients while game effects are captured through
CommandQueue.
